WEBVTT


00:02:20.680 --> 00:02:24.513
You're dead! You're fucking dead!


00:02:24.599 --> 00:02:26.078
I'll get my brother!


00:02:26.159 --> 00:02:30.471
- Jen, come back! Wait!
- Fucking pervert!


00:02:30.559 --> 00:02:34.552
If that was a joke,
it wasn't very fucking funny.


00:02:34.639 --> 00:02:37.437
I'd look out for her brother.
He's a fucking mentalist.


00:02:37.519 --> 00:02:40.430
Jen! Jen!


00:03:57.793 --> 00:04:00.943
- I'll miss you.
- I hate you.


00:04:01.032 --> 00:04:04.503
Can I take this?
This can't still fit you, surely?


00:04:04.593 --> 00:04:07.345
- Get out of my room, Hallam.
- Not without these.


00:04:07.432 --> 00:04:09.150
- Hallam!
- I'm gonna take these,


00:04:09.233 --> 00:04:11.792
- and what if I put these back? Ow!
- Get out of my room.


00:05:27.267 --> 00:05:28.255
Thank you.


00:05:29.266 --> 00:05:33.145
To Australia and great adventures.


00:05:33.227 --> 00:05:35.296
And happy anniversary, Dad and Verity.


00:05:36.186 --> 00:05:38.222
Absent friends.


00:05:39.545 --> 00:05:40.534
Absent friends.


00:05:47.305 --> 00:05:49.660
Do you know why
we chose this restaurant?


00:05:49.745 --> 00:05:53.021
- It can't be the food.
- I told you to have the veal.


00:05:53.105 --> 00:05:58.098
It was here that Julius first
asked me to help manage the firm.


00:05:58.184 --> 00:06:01.335
You mean when you were the secretary?


00:06:01.424 --> 00:06:03.892
That's right, when I was his secretary.


00:06:03.984 --> 00:06:06.976
- I didn't know that.
- That's because I said no.


00:06:07.064 --> 00:06:08.383
I wasn't ready for it then.


00:06:08.464 --> 00:06:11.023
This afternoon,
I put the same question to Verity,


00:06:11.103 --> 00:06:13.901
- and I'm happy to say she agreed.
- Congratulations.


00:06:18.343 --> 00:06:20.299
When was it you were first asked?


00:06:22.062 --> 00:06:24.019
It must have been
a couple of years ago.


00:06:24.103 --> 00:06:26.741
And was that before or after?


00:06:29.782 --> 00:06:32.171
It wasn't long
before your mother passed away.


00:06:42.381 --> 00:06:45.737
Do you remember what happened later?
Your friend.


00:06:45.821 --> 00:06:49.655
Oh, yes.


00:06:49.741 --> 00:06:52.174
That same day,
an old boyfriend of mine calls up


00:06:52.260 --> 00:06:56.253
and insists on taking me out
for dinner. Guess where he took me.


00:06:56.340 --> 00:07:00.252
Can you imagine
what the staff must have thought?


00:07:00.339 --> 00:07:03.776
They probably
thought you were a prostitute.


00:07:11.859 --> 00:07:13.292
Probably.


00:07:18.738 --> 00:07:22.618
- Come to the pub.
- No, thanks. Here's fine.


00:07:22.699 --> 00:07:25.496
You got your binoculars in there?


00:07:25.578 --> 00:07:28.808
- Come to the pub.
- Maybe next time.


00:07:28.898 --> 00:07:31.855
There isn't gonna be a next time.


00:07:36.617 --> 00:07:38.812
You fucking splitter.


00:09:14.610 --> 00:09:16.168
Night, Mum.


00:09:26.490 --> 00:09:28.605
Hallam!


00:09:29.729 --> 00:09:31.640
I'm going!


00:09:33.928 --> 00:09:35.999
Bye!


00:09:46.527 --> 00:09:47.881
Lucy!


00:09:50.408 --> 00:09:53.683
Wait! Lucy!


00:10:23.366 --> 00:10:25.959
Hallam, lunch is ready.


00:10:34.365 --> 00:10:36.242
It's very good soup.


00:10:38.924 --> 00:10:41.154
We've been thinking,
now that Lucy's gone,


00:10:41.244 --> 00:10:45.795
it's not good for you to be here
with no one of your own age around.


00:10:47.324 --> 00:10:50.713
Too much time to dwell on things.


00:10:50.803 --> 00:10:54.000
I have some contacts
in the wine trade in London, and...


00:10:54.083 --> 00:10:57.359
You'll have a chance to make
new friends, earn a bit of money,


00:10:57.443 --> 00:11:00.037
learn something you'll enjoy
the rest of your life,


00:11:00.123 --> 00:11:02.842
and it'll be a good
stop-gap before college.


00:11:02.923 --> 00:11:05.800
Actually, I've decided
not to go to college.


00:11:05.882 --> 00:11:10.034
- So what are you going to do?
- I'm staying right here.


00:11:10.962 --> 00:11:13.920
So I'm sorry if that
screws up your plans.


00:12:23.757 --> 00:12:25.986
It's as if this place is still hers.


00:12:26.076 --> 00:12:29.751
We agreed you could make
whatever changes you want, and you are.


00:12:29.836 --> 00:12:32.669
- You know what I want most?
- What?


00:12:37.595 --> 00:12:39.552
- Look, he doesn't hate you.
- He does.


00:12:39.636 --> 00:12:43.150
He doesn't. You just have to be patient.


00:12:47.035 --> 00:12:49.310
I think that
I should go away for a while.


00:12:53.314 --> 00:12:56.465
I'll deal with Hallam. All right?


00:13:17.753 --> 00:13:22.143
- Where's Verity?
- She's gone to see a friend.


00:13:24.352 --> 00:13:26.024
Are you in the dog house?


00:13:28.112 --> 00:13:29.942
What is it, Hallam?


00:13:30.031 --> 00:13:32.704
- I found Mum's old boat in the loch.
- Did you?


00:13:32.791 --> 00:13:37.387
- Good God! I thought it was sunk.
- It had.


00:13:37.471 --> 00:13:41.258
When she took me out in it,
how long was that before she died?


00:13:41.351 --> 00:13:43.228
About a month. Why?


00:13:43.311 --> 00:13:45.347
Were you fucking Verity by then?


00:13:47.390 --> 00:13:50.462
That's what "Fancy a stroll"
was about. Christ, I'm a fool.


00:13:50.550 --> 00:13:53.587
- You haven't answered the question.
- Not even close, Hal.


00:13:53.670 --> 00:13:55.945
I was busy trying
to keep the show on the road.


00:13:56.030 --> 00:13:59.340
When you found her, had she tied
her hands and weighed herself down?


00:13:59.430 --> 00:14:01.863
- Where's this coming from?
- People who can swim,


00:14:01.950 --> 00:14:04.338
it's hard to drown. Instincts take over.


00:14:04.429 --> 00:14:09.549
- Who told you that?
- I did some research, all right?


00:14:11.829 --> 00:14:16.266
At the time, I decided to spare you
some of the details from the inquest.


00:14:19.588 --> 00:14:23.263
Before she came out here,


00:14:23.348 --> 00:14:27.056
your mother took
an overdose of sleeping pills.


00:14:30.947 --> 00:14:35.020
- Thanks for fucking telling me.
- I'm sorry.


00:14:36.147 --> 00:14:40.425
I know it's hard, but you
have got to try to pick up the pieces.


00:14:40.507 --> 00:14:43.067
Well, I can see it didn't
take you very long, did it?


00:14:43.147 --> 00:14:45.660
Hal, this won't help.


00:14:50.306 --> 00:14:52.296
So it definitely wasn't an accident?


00:14:53.785 --> 00:14:55.298
No.


00:14:56.705 --> 00:14:57.934
It wasn't.


00:15:32.583 --> 00:15:36.416
Oh, no! I've painted
over his mum's face.


00:15:36.502 --> 00:15:38.220
Paint all over it.


00:15:38.302 --> 00:15:41.180
- Give it here, I'll do it.
- It's a single ticket.


00:15:45.142 --> 00:15:47.098
Fuck off, man. Go!


00:17:02.577 --> 00:17:04.726
<i>- Hallam?
- Lucy?</i>


00:17:07.776 --> 00:17:10.414
<i>- Are you still there? Hello?
- Can you hear me?</i>


00:17:14.416 --> 00:17:19.091
What if someone else gave her the pills?
Spiked her drink or something?


00:17:19.775 --> 00:17:22.687
Well, don't you think
she's capable of it?


00:17:22.775 --> 00:17:24.731
Why is that paranoid?


00:17:26.615 --> 00:17:29.687
Of course I miss you.
Oh, she'd love that.


00:17:29.775 --> 00:17:32.926
She's already twisting Dad's arm
to try and get rid of me.


00:18:42.009 --> 00:18:43.761
Hello!


00:18:46.569 --> 00:18:48.685
I see you've had some visitors.


00:18:49.369 --> 00:18:51.484
- Can I come up?
- No way.


00:19:13.607 --> 00:19:15.483
You left these on your bed.


00:19:18.927 --> 00:19:23.522
"Today, walking past the office,
I saw Dad stroking Verity's back.


00:19:23.607 --> 00:19:25.642
It made me ponder his evening strolls".


00:19:25.726 --> 00:19:27.478
- Not allowed.
- "I followed.


00:19:27.566 --> 00:19:31.353
There she was, bouncing up and down.
I couldn't take my eyes off the dimple


00:19:31.445 --> 00:19:36.200
that appeared on her shoulder
every time she clawed at his neck.


00:19:36.286 --> 00:19:41.882
I hate myself, but I want to
bury my face in that little cushion".


00:19:41.965 --> 00:19:44.080
Give me my diaries back.


00:19:44.165 --> 00:19:46.599
Hallam, you really need to move on.


00:19:46.684 --> 00:19:49.324
I know Julius will feel the same
when he reads these.


00:19:49.405 --> 00:19:51.042
No, they're private diaries!


00:19:51.124 --> 00:19:54.400
So are bedrooms. By volume two,
you peeped in half the village's.


00:19:54.484 --> 00:19:57.681
I wonder what the local paper
would do with that,


00:19:57.764 --> 00:20:00.756
- or the police for that matter.
- The police?


00:20:00.843 --> 00:20:03.563
Wonder what they'll think
when I tell them about you.


00:20:03.644 --> 00:20:05.281
Me?


00:20:06.524 --> 00:20:08.673
Recognise this?


00:20:08.763 --> 00:20:09.991
It's a hammer, Hallam.


00:20:10.083 --> 00:20:14.315
The same hammer that sunk my mother's
boat once you'd drugged her coffee.


00:20:22.402 --> 00:20:24.996
She wanted to die, Hallam.


00:20:25.081 --> 00:20:27.596
You tell me what you did to her!


00:21:56.715 --> 00:21:59.752
It's time to fly the nest, Hallam,


00:21:59.835 --> 00:22:01.790
and I think you know that.


00:22:52.311 --> 00:22:54.541
Spare some change, please.


00:24:23.305 --> 00:24:27.058
- It's a fucking shite hole.
- I didn't want to come here.


00:24:27.144 --> 00:24:30.420
Stick your fucking castle
right up your fucking arse.


00:24:30.504 --> 00:24:32.813
What do you want?


00:24:32.904 --> 00:24:35.099
Thirty, 35?


00:24:35.944 --> 00:24:37.297
Thirty-five?


00:24:39.583 --> 00:24:42.144
Well, go on, fuck off, then!


00:24:42.224 --> 00:24:43.372
Fuck off, then!


00:24:44.623 --> 00:24:46.454
Whoa.


00:24:46.543 --> 00:24:49.296
- What's your name, son?
- Carl.


00:24:49.383 --> 00:24:53.011
- Where's home, Carl?
- I'm staying with a friend.


00:24:53.102 --> 00:24:55.139
Not that gentleman
you were talking to?


00:24:55.222 --> 00:24:59.215
- No.
- So, your friend, what's his address?


00:25:26.140 --> 00:25:28.779
Where the hell is he?


00:26:27.616 --> 00:26:29.173
Mum!


00:27:47.010 --> 00:27:48.568
Can I help you?


00:27:53.649 --> 00:27:55.879
Do you have any jobs, please?


00:27:55.969 --> 00:27:58.961
Sorry, we use an agency.
I can give you their details.


00:27:59.049 --> 00:28:00.528
Thanks.


00:28:08.728 --> 00:28:10.719
Why are you staring at me?


00:28:10.808 --> 00:28:14.847
I'm sorry. I didn't mean to. I've never
been for a job interview before,


00:28:14.928 --> 00:28:18.966
and I was just wondering if you could
give me some advice on how to do it.


00:28:19.047 --> 00:28:22.802
- I'm sorry?
- Would you...?


00:28:22.887 --> 00:28:26.038
Could you throw a couple
of practise questions at me, just...


00:28:26.127 --> 00:28:27.719
...just for practise?


00:28:30.847 --> 00:28:34.999
- How desperate are you for work?
- Pretty desperate.


00:28:35.087 --> 00:28:38.965
Well, the highest turnover in jobs
is usually in kitchen porters.


00:28:39.046 --> 00:28:42.516
- OK. I'll be a kitchen porter.
- Why do you think you'd be suitable?


00:28:42.606 --> 00:28:45.518
Well, it's what I've wanted to do
ever since I was a kid.


00:28:45.605 --> 00:28:47.323
Sit down.


00:28:49.885 --> 00:28:53.002
Don't tell people
what you think they want to hear.


00:28:53.085 --> 00:28:55.804
- Just be yourself.
- OK.


00:28:55.885 --> 00:28:58.922
I'm very enthusiastic
and I'm a quick learner,


00:28:59.005 --> 00:29:01.155
and I'll work days, nights, weekends,


00:29:01.244 --> 00:29:03.314
any overtime you want
for no extra money.


00:29:03.404 --> 00:29:07.716
It would be illegal for you
to work overtime for no extra money.


00:29:07.804 --> 00:29:10.193
Well, give me a week's trial,
a day's trial.


00:29:10.284 --> 00:29:12.434
I want a chance
to get a foot on the ladder.


00:29:12.524 --> 00:29:15.322
If everything works out,
you won't pay agency fees.


00:29:15.404 --> 00:29:18.315
That's a win-win situation for you.


00:29:24.363 --> 00:29:28.355
Remember what I said about
the fast turnover in kitchen porters?


00:29:29.403 --> 00:29:32.236
You're about to meet the exception.


00:29:33.282 --> 00:29:36.911
- Cutlery, handles up.
- Right.


00:29:37.002 --> 00:29:38.275
Go on.


00:29:41.281 --> 00:29:45.832
Hey, hey, hey! What is the hurry?
Trying to show me up on your first day?


00:29:45.921 --> 00:29:47.559
No.


00:29:47.641 --> 00:29:51.873
I fucking hate this job,
but it's my job.


00:29:51.961 --> 00:29:53.440
Do you understand?


00:29:55.041 --> 00:29:56.871
I killed a man once.


00:29:56.960 --> 00:29:59.350
Smashed his skull on a pier.


00:30:00.480 --> 00:30:01.993
Just so you know.


00:30:21.679 --> 00:30:24.238
You take the rest. I'm off for a smoke.


00:32:44.429 --> 00:32:47.898
Don't make friends with the chefs,
otherwise they'll want favours.


00:32:47.988 --> 00:32:49.819
But don't get on their bad side,


00:32:49.908 --> 00:32:53.696
or you'll be cleaning out
the fat fryer on a quiet Thursday.


00:32:54.428 --> 00:32:58.467
They're all cunts anyway.
Except TJ. He's OK.


00:32:58.548 --> 00:33:00.458
Even if he is a fucking bullshitter.


00:33:00.547 --> 00:33:04.586
Have you ever met an African over here
who wasn't a brain surgeon over there?


00:33:04.667 --> 00:33:07.385
Are you listening to me?


00:33:09.307 --> 00:33:11.740
Yes, of course.


00:33:11.826 --> 00:33:14.943
Brain surgeon. African. Cunt.


00:33:15.026 --> 00:33:17.938
Aye, cunt.


00:33:33.665 --> 00:33:37.134
Reach out. One, two.
One. Right knee.


00:38:40.242 --> 00:38:42.837
- Hey! Ho!
- Raymond!


00:38:42.922 --> 00:38:44.514
- Hey!
- Hey!


00:38:44.602 --> 00:38:48.561
Oh-ho! That's gonna cost you.


00:38:48.642 --> 00:38:50.758
- Really?
- Yeah.


00:38:54.481 --> 00:38:58.270
- Are you serious?
- Absolutely.


00:39:06.001 --> 00:39:07.559
Come on. You're losing.


00:39:13.641 --> 00:39:15.039
That's ¡Ì4.


00:39:19.120 --> 00:39:22.157
- Do you mind if I take a break?
- Do what the fuck you like.

